WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.060
Nama saya... Paul
["My name is Paul" in Indonesian]

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.600
[bad indonesian]

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:14.340
Man, I've been studying Indonesian 
for six months and 17 days.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:17.160
And I still can't introduce myself.
What's going on here?

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:24.800
Hi guys, this is Paul.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:27.940
Today I want to talk to you about 
one of the most important...

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:31.100
elements of learning a language, 
of studying a language.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.000
And that is consistency.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.260
This is one of my moto: 
consistency is king

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:39.960
If you've read my blog or something 
you've heard, talked to me about languages,

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:44.920
you probably heard me say that slogan,
that motto: consistency is king.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:51.380
The people who really get good at languages
are the people who study consistently.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:53.840
They study everyday, come hell or high water.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:56.800
They don't find excuse to skip their studying

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:03.640
The people who don't really learn as much,
the people who don't get that good, 
the people who learned just a bit,

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.060
Those are the people who just study
whenever they feel like it.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:10.880
The people who don't study consistently,
they just study based on a whim.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:14.580
So I like to think about consistency in a couple of ways.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:16.700
The first way is like this:

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:22.000
Your language ability is like a bucket 
with a small hole in the bottom.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:26.600
Right? So the water, the liquid inside 
is your language ability.

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:30.280
And if you stop studying, 
then there's a slow leak and...

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:34.280
your ability will slowly diminish 
if you don't top up the bucket.

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:40.820
But, if you top up the bucket, everyday by studying,
then you can maintain the level consistently.

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:45.280
you can maintain a certain level or even
raise the level of the liquid inside the bucket.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:50.180
But it's when you stop studying, when you're not 
consistent, then gradually, day by day,

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:54.700
each day a little bit of the liquid leaks out
the bottom and the level diminishes

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:57.020
So that's like your language ability going down.

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:02.320
So if you've ever studied the language for a couple 
of months and then you took a few weeks off,

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:06.880
like maybe you lost motivation or whatever, 
then you came back to it you probably noticed

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:12.360
if you probably felt that you had lost 
the majority of what you have learned. Right?

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:18.300
So that's because you had that little bit of liquid 
in the bucket and then it gradually mostly leaked out

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:21.540
There is probably some residue in there, 
a few drops but...

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:27.560
you probably lost a lot of the meat of
what you had learned. So that's 1 example.

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:32.620
If you've ever been a couple years into studying 
a language, like a year or two,

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:39.600
And then, you took a few weeks off, you probably 
noticed that your level had diminished a bit.
Probably it had gone down but...

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:43.060
You probably didn't feel like you've lost
most of what you learned

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:48.220
because it's that gradual diminishment. 
It's that gradual lowering of the level. It's a slow leak.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:54.320
So the more of a beginner you are, the more 
of your ability you will lose, if you're not consistent.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:03:02.160
But the way to always maintain your level and 
to keep increasing it is to be consistent 
and top up the bucket everyday.

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:06.780
So that's one way I like to think about it,
your consistency in studying.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:15.120
The other way I like to think about it is in terms
of investing. When you invest money over time,

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:19.720
when you do it consistently, 
you can gain compound interest. Right?

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:26.340
That means that you make interest on the money that
you invest but then you make interest on the interest as well.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:31.380
This is similar to a phenomena 
that I've noticed when studying consistently.

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:35.860
When you study every day consistently,
you don't take days off,

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:43.620
your learning kind of takes on a life of its own and 
you end up learning more than you would expect
from the amount you're studying. Right?

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:52.820
That's partly because, if your brain is learning 
in the off time, when you're not studying, it's kind 
of processing things in the background all day.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:57.800
But basically, if you are consistent, 
then you can get your...

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:02.680
you are learning to a sort of critical mass
where it starts to take on a life of its own.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:08.380
You learn more than you would have if you'd studied 
that same number of days but with breaks in between.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:14.020
So it's really important to... 
to always keep investing on a daily basis,

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:18.300
investing regularly so that you can get
that compounding effect in your learning.

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:22.580
Okay so, that's another way I like to think about it. 
So there's the the bucket with the hole in the bottom

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:25.260
but then there's compounding interest. 
So those are the two ways.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:29.820
So the most important point 
is study everyday, be consistent.

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:34.420
Also put in a certain amount of time everyday, 
try to commit as much time to it as you can but...

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:38.120
more important than that 
is to do it consistently everyday.

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:41.640
How do you be consistent?
That's the question that remains.

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:47.980
A lot of people intend to be consistent but they end up 
taking a lot of time off and being inconsistent.

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:55.300
So those people usually are taking action based 
on how they feel at the moment.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:05:00.320
Right? They wake up in the morning 
and they think "oh I'm tired today,
screw it, i just won't study today"

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:04.720
They're basing their action 
on the feeling of that moment,

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:08.720
which is something you can't really control. 
The way you feel depends on...

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:14.420
all sorts of different factors out of your control,
depends on maybe what you ate yesterday.

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:17.440
It depends on the weather.
It depends on how well you slept.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:22.420
It depends on stress at work, all these things. 
So you can't really control it that easily.

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:25.860
Unless you're always monitoring 
all those things really closely.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:30.020
So the way to the way to take action
should be based on...

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:35.540
your vision for your outcome, what you want to get 
out of learning that language.

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:38.080
And also based on just the commitment.

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:40.860
Commitment to achieving that outcome,
achieving that vision.

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:44.860
So let's say you want to be a French-English 
translator,  that's your dream.

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:49.200
So you have to have that vision in mind for the future, 
that goal, what will that look like.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:53.820
And then a commitment to work hard
 everyday to achieve that. Right?

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:56.640
So that, in that case, if you have 
that vision and commitment,

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:00.460
when you wake up in the morning and you're tired 
or hungover or whatever,

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:04.420
then you will just tell yourself: 
"Okay, I don't feel like it today but...

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:09.020
I have that vision and the commitment. So I'm going 
to do it anyway because it's not based on the feeling.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:13.580
So that's how you...
that's how you can be consistent is by doing that.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:19.300
Alright, don't let it be based on a feeling. A feeling is...
changing by the moment, it's out of your control.

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:24.060
Base it on your vision and commitment.
Alright, I hope that's helpful.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:26.820
Thank you very much for listening 
and 'talk to you again...

